  "body": "The focus fixup rule should reset focus to body in the modal case, and no element will be focused in the non-modal case. So the behavior stays the same after and before this PR in terms of focused element\n\n<!--\nThank you for contributing to the HTML Standard! Please describe the change you are making and complete the checklist below if your change is not editorial.\n-->\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n   * Webkit\n  * Chromium: https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/html/html_dialog_element.cc;l=48;drc=f4b6354a57a403a0b56b940104013cda4c37a7af\n  * Gecko: https://searchfox.org/mozilla-central/rev/553bf8428885dbd1eab9b63f71ef647f799372c2/dom/html/HTMLDialogElement.cpp#149 \n- [x] [Tests](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt) are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n   * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/31724\n- [x] [Implementation bugs](https://github.com/whatwg/meta/blob/main/MAINTAINERS.md#handling-pull-requests) are filed:\n   * Chrome: N/A\n   * Firefox: N/A\n   * Safari: TODO\n\n(See [WHATWG Working Mode: Changes](https://whatwg.org/working-mode#changes) for more details.)\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7366/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 24, 2021, 8:49 PM UTC (4aefbcd)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7366/8265358...4aefbcd/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 24, 2021, 8:49 PM UTC (4aefbcd)\">diff</a> )\n<a